{"_data": [{"type": "metadata", "contents": [{"content": "New Challenges", "type": "lesson_name"}, {"content": "The Gala", "type": "unit_name"}, {"content": 10, "type": "position"}, {"content": "stub", "type": "origin"}, {"content": 9, "type": "lesson"}, {"content": "B2.3", "type": "level"}]}, {"type": "achievment_test", "contents": [{"content": "false", "type": "test"}]}, {"type": "objectives", "contents": [{"content": "Describe the reasons or results of events or actions in spoken or written texts, in work and social contexts.", "type": "primary"}, {"content": "Integrates factual information to a wider range of written and spoken language skills and knowledge in the workplace.", "type": "secondary_1"}, {"content": "Integrates factual information to a wider range of written and spoken language skills and knowledge in the workplace.", "type": "secondary_2"}, {"content": "Integrates factual information to a wider range of written and spoken language skills and knowledge in the workplace.", "type": "secondary_3"}, {"content": "Integrates factual information to a wider range of written and spoken language skills and knowledge in the workplace.", "type": "secondary_4"}, {"content": "Integrates factual information to a wider range of written and spoken language skills and knowledge in the workplace.", "type": "secondary_5"}, {"content": "Integrates factual information to a wider range of written and spoken language skills and knowledge in the workplace.", "type": "secondary_6"}, {"content": "Integrates factual information to a wider range of written and spoken language skills and knowledge in the workplace.", "type": "secondary_7"}, {"content": "Integrates factual information to a wider range of written and spoken language skills and knowledge in the workplace.", "type": "secondary_8"}]}, {"content": "engenn11le09ob10re1img01.jpg", "type": "background_image"}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "Result Clauses", "type": "heading"}, {"content": " You use linking words when you want to introduce clauses that express results. Linking words help you connect the ideas in a sentence. ", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "A common linking phrase that you use in result clauses is <span class=\"italic\">so</span>.<br/><span class=\"italic\">So</span> introduces the result of something. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "For example:", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<span class=\"italic\">I am very nervous. <span class=\"strong\">So</span>, I may need something a little stronger.</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "You can use <span class=\"italic\">as a result</span> to introduce a result.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "For example:", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<span class=\"italic\"><span class=\"strong\">As a result</span> of them winning the lottery, they took us to Barbados.</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "You use <span class=\"italic\">therefore</span> and <span class=\"italic\">consequently</span> at the beginning of sentences to introduce a result.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "For example:", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<span class=\"italic\">First, the manager verifies that everyone has had their police check. <span class=\"strong\">Therefore</span>, we won't have to deal with any surprises. </span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<span class=\"italic\">Second, make sure we have enough food and drink for everyone. <span class=\"strong\">Consequently</span>, everyone will be happy. </span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<span class=\"strong\">As a result</span> of everything going well, is it time to mingle?", "type": "example"}, {"content": "First, we do a sweep to make sure everything is set up properly. <span class=\"strong\">Therefore</span>, there are no surprises. ", "type": "example"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "Reason Clauses ", "type": "heading"}, {"content": " When you want to refer to the reason for something, you can use reason clauses introduced by a linking word. ", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "Some common linking words you use in reason clauses are:<br/> <span class=\"italic\">because</span>, <span class=\"italic\">since</span>, <span class=\"italic\">as</span>, and <span class=\"italic\">so</span>.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<span class=\"underline\">Because </span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "When you use <span class=\"italic\">because</span> to introduce a reason, you use it with a subject and a verb.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "For example:", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<span class=\"italic\">I'm really thrilled to be here <span class=\"strong\">because I have always dreamed of being a filmmaker</span>.</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<span class=\"underline\">Since/As </span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<span class=\"italic\">Since</span> and <span class=\"italic\">as</span> are more informal, and they are followed by a subject  and a verb.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "For example:", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<span class=\"italic\"><span class=\"strong\">As you are the director of the movie</span>, you'll be expected to communicate your vision to the producers.<br/>Provide the cast with lots of healthy food <span class=\"strong\">since they will be working hard all day without many breaks</span>.</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "You can use <span class=\"italic\">just in case</span> as a linking phrase. It means \u201cin the case that\u201d.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "For example:", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<span class=\"italic\"> Prepare 50 extra seats <span class=\"strong\">just in case some unexpected guests arrive</span>.</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I'm so excited because this is all so new to me.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "Help her with anything she needs since she is the guest of honor.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "As you are the star of the show, we'll need you to say a few words.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "Copy 100 just in case we have unexpected guests.", "type": "example"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "gang", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a group of friends, co-workers ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Ok. Gang, let's split up.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn11le09ob10aud01", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"content": "These are words you use when organizing an event.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "running smoothly", "type": "name"}, {"content": "happening without problems", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Everything looks like it is running smoothly.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn11le09ob10aud02", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "sweep", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a \u200bmovement, \u200bespecially a \u200bquick one to check for things ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: First, we do a sweep to make sure everything is set up properly. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn11le09ob10aud03", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to shepherd", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to lead people somewhere", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: After that, shepherd Marisa.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn11le09ob10aud04", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "brochure", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a small book or magazine containing pictures and information about a product or service", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example:  Adam we need more brochures so that we can pass them out to the guests.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn11le09ob10aud05", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"content": "Imagine that you are on the committee responsible for planning the holiday office party at work.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Brainstorm a list of things you need to consider for the party.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Include details about the following aspects: the date and time, invitations and guest list, location, food/drinks, budget and music/entertainment.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Discuss your ideas in groups and explain your decisions.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Make a final decision on the details for the holiday office party.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"content": "I brainstorm ideas for a holiday office party where I work.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I make a list of things necessary for the party.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I discuss different aspects of the party in a group.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I come to a decision with my group about the details for the party.", "type": "text"}]}], "type": "sena", "labs": [{"_data": [{"type": "lab_options", "contents": [{"content": true, "type": "has_nav"}, {"content": true, "type": "has_exercise_controls"}]}], "exercises": [{"stimuli_ids": [0], "img_path": "", "id": 0, "_data": [{"type": "instructions", "contents": [{"content": " I can discuss reasons and results of an event or action related to work and jobs.", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": " I can express willingness or intention to do something in work and job issues.", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": " I can exchange complex professional information related to work and job issues.", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": " Have you tried to organize an event before? What kind?", "type": "Free Header Item"}, {"content": " Are you good at small talk? Do you like to mingle at parties? Why or why not?", "type": "Free Header Item"}]}, {"type": "group", "contents": [{"content": "Welcome", "type": "group_name"}]